DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260516T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260516T150000
UID:69d802b0b6c4ac1fedcb4a14@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Love a challenge? Or just want to participate in a relaxing ac
 tivity? Join us for a relaxing puzzle day! Kids can come and build jigsaw 
 puzzles\, in groups or alone\, and challenge themselves.\nDrop-in. For age
 s 4-12 only.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69d802b0b6c4ac1fedcb4a14
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Family Chess
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260527T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260527T173000
UID:69d8026be2a2952aed0dbbac@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a chess adventure! Learn the basics\, challenge fr
 iends and family\, and discover new strategies as you play. Whether you're
  just starting or already thinking a few moves ahead\, come play\, learn\,
  and have fun together.\nFor ages 6-12. Caregivers are welcome to particip
 ate.\nDrop-in.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69d8026be2a2952aed0dbbac
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Unconventional Materials: An Osborne Collection Exhibit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260316T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260531T235959
UID:698cfed31e64afd01e5acb6d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:An exhibition of intricately crafted books\, artworks and much
  more. The Unconventional Materials exhibit highlights the use of unconven
 tional techniques and materials in children’s literature\, featuring his
 torical and modern examples.\nVisit the Osborne Collection to experience o
 ur exhibit featuring items such as plasticine art by Barbara Reid\, dioram
 as and panoramas\, postcards and other ephemera\, and hornbooks and battle
 dores.\nLocated on the 4th floor of the Lillian H. Smith Branch. Free. All
  are welcome. Registration is not required.\nThe exhibit can be viewed dur
 ing the Osborne Collection's open hours. Contact the Osborne Collection at
  416-393-7753 or email osstaff@tpl.ca for more information.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Osborne Collection of Early Children's Books. 
 4th floor. The exhibit is open during the same hours as the branch.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698cfed31e64afd01e5acb6d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
