 r School Club and learn new things\, make stuff\, meet other kids and have
  fun! For ages\n[\n6-12].\nSnacks are offered during the After School Club
  for participants. Ingredient lists will be available. Snacks are generous
 ly supported\, in part\, by donors.\nMonday\, May 11:\nThis program is in
  honour of Asian Heritage Month!  Artist Sharon Kawabata demonstrates & t
 eaches how to turn scrap paper\, old magazines\, & ads into classic origa
 mi pieces: crane\, butterfly\, fish\, boats\, water birds\, & more\, relat
 ing to immigration from Japan to Canada (with a display of physical artifa
 cts dating from 1900s British\nColumbia).\nAll materials will be provided!
