DESCRIPTION:Artist Sharon Kawabata demonstrates and teaches how to turn sc
 rap paper\, old magazines/ads into classic origami pieces: bird\, butterfl
 y\, fish\, etc\, using local animals for inspiration and the creation of a
 nimal origami as the primary projects.\nPaper folding can be a relaxing pr
 ocess\, like many crafts once the skill has been acquired repetition may b
 e a calming result. ​\nFor school-aged children and their caregivers. Al
 l materials provided. Drop-in.\nMaximum of 20 participants. Participants c
 an join until 4:15pm.\nUnfortunately\, we cannot accommodate any large gro
 ups/daycares for this program.\nIf you identify as a person with a disabil
 ity and require an accessibility accommodation to participate in this prog
 ram\, please contact Accessibility Services by email\, accessibleservices@
